  "body": "MAINLINE-036 complete. No matched minimum compressive yield for finished thin SR-200 faces was established. The maker's 345 MPa minimum is tensile; inspected MIL-HDBK-5J/MMPDS sheet Fcy cells are blank. Historical thicker-sheet compression supports plausibility, not gauge/process/biaxial qualification. PS-200/PF-60 catalogs add no compression basis.\n\nHeld R10 requirements are 300.333 MPa for the scarf routes and 321.580 MPa for light bond/ideal weld. Held R20 requires 338.744 MPa face stress and 376.382 MPa material strength with its 0.9 joint efficiency. Re-optimization preserves each predecessor's pressure, reserves and joining law.\n\nWith full projected gamma/wrinkling and catalog E=290 GPa, R10 minimum strengths are 298.906 MPa nominal scarf, 300.135 primer, and 298.257 light-bond routes. R20 needs 375.839 MPa under original elastic inputs, or 381.612 MPa with handbook sheet scalar elasticity; historical 379.2 then yields only SF=0.994817. Scalar elasticity is itself unvalidated for the formed orthotropic hull.\n\nCompression qualification is an additional unresolved material assumption. Existing buckling, wrinkling and joining assumptions remain open; installed-hull SF is unknown. Gauge tolerances and additional finishing are treated separately without double-counting etch.\n\nSeventeen input pins and 218 checks passed; 14 evidence rows and 15 NFI items filed. Brief names no successor: stop and file, awaiting robotics' next queued job.",
